Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> expression
Rule 1     expression -> expression PLUS term
Rule 2     expression -> expression MINUS term
Rule 3     expression -> term
Rule 4     term -> term TIMES factor
Rule 5     term -> term DIVIDE factor
Rule 6     term -> term POWER factor
Rule 7     term -> factor
Rule 8     factor -> NUMBER
Rule 9     factor -> VARIABLE
Rule 10    factor -> CONSTANT
Rule 11    factor -> FUNCTION PAREN_OPEN arg_list PAREN_CLOSE
Rule 12    factor -> PAREN_OPEN expression PAREN_CLOSE
Rule 13    factor -> MINUS factor
Rule 14    factor -> PLUS factor
Rule 15    arg_list -> expression
Rule 16    arg_list -> arg_list COMMA expression

Terminals, with rules where they appear

COMMA                : 16
CONSTANT             : 10
DIVIDE               : 5
FUNCTION             : 11
MINUS                : 2 13
NUMBER               : 8
PAREN_CLOSE          : 11 12
PAREN_OPEN           : 11 12
PLUS                 : 1 14
POWER                : 6
TIMES                : 4
VARIABLE             : 9
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

arg_list             : 11 16
expression           : 1 2 12 15 16 0
factor               : 4 5 6 7 13 14
term                 : 1 2 3 4 5 6

Parsing method: LALR

